Package: rcapsule
Title: Reproducibility Capsules and Multi-Target Containerization for R
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R:
    person("Marcus", "Harris", , "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Compiles R analysis projects, 'Quarto' manuscripts, 'R Markdown'
    reports, R packages, 'targets' pipelines, and 'Shiny' applications into
    lean, layer-cached 'Docker' files, multi-service 'docker-compose.yml'
    stacks, and HPC-ready 'Apptainer' definitions. Resolves full-stack R
    package, OS system library, and scientific toolchain dependencies
    ('CmdStan', 'TMB', 'RTMB', 'JAGS', 'C++', 'Rust', 'Python', 'reticulate',
    'Quarto', and 'LaTeX'), records cryptographically verifiable provenance
    manifests ('capsule.json') with 'SHA-256' artifact hashes and optional
    'HMAC-SHA256' signatures, exports and validates 'CycloneDX' 1.5 Software
    Bills of Materials ('SBOM'), compares runs across machines, diagnoses
    reproducibility drift with ranked remediations, exports journal-ready
    peer-review bundles and HPC container descriptors, and executes isolated
    reproducibility and script audits with exact and numeric-tolerance
    comparators to produce verification certificates.
